<h2> What is the web actually? </h2>

   <p> The World Wide Web is a system that allows people to access and
                share information through websites and web pages. It was
                invented by Tim Berners-Lee in 1989.  The Web is a way of accessing information through the Internet.
                Websites are connected to each other using hyperlinks, which
                makes it possible to move from one page to another. </p>
    
  <h2> How websites work</h2>
   
  <p>  Websites are created using different technologies. HTML is used
                to structure the content of a webpage, CSS can be used to
                control how the page looks, and JavaScript can make the page
                interactive.  When you visit a website, your browser requests information
                from a web server. The server sends the website back to your
                browser, which displays it on your screen.</p>

  
  <h2> What I have learned this week</h2>
  <ul>
    <li> I have learned about the very basics of HTML.</li>
    <li> I have learned that p is used to create paragraphs and h1 is used to create headings.</li>
    <li> I have learned how to use lists in HTML.</li>
    <li> I have learned how to create links in HTML.</li>
    <li> I have learned how to add images to a website.</li>
  </ul>

   <h2> What I like about this course </h2>
